{
  "name": "place-declaration-hold-declare",
  "description": "The page sets the theme, declares the view composition of the surface that is mounted, and sends a layout of that surface while it leaves the surface that is not mounted out; the host answers the layout with its ticket and the chrome row, and only after that answer the page declares the view composition of the surface that was left out.",
  "replay": false,
  "reason": "setTheme, compositionDeclare and syncSurfaces apply the theme, the views and the placement of the native window, and only the native host with a window produces their replies (docs/operations/examples.md#test-kinds).",
